-- title:
--   Unramified nonempty level sets of the modular unit mod q
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ be a nonzero natural number and $q$ a prime not dividing $N_0$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` for the curve `X N₀ q` over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring `R q` (a bundle consisting of properness, flatness, integrality and local finite presentation of the structure map, integral closedness of the sections on affine opens, a smooth proper curve model over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with function field the base change of `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)` together with its identification with the geometric fibre and its Galois equivariance, smoothness of relative dimension $1$ and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, and cusp sections). Write $A$ for `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q`, the subalgebra of $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)` of elements integral over the $\mathbb Z_{(q)}$-subalgebra generated by `jFull`. Let $u\in A$ be an element whose Laurent series in $F\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb Q$ is `modularUnitSeries q` $=\Delta\cdot\Delta_q^{-1}$, and let $P\subset A$ be a prime ideal minimal over the ideal generated by $q$ with $u\notin P$. Then there is a nonzero polynomial $\mathrm{avoid}\in(\mathbb Z/q)[X]$ such that for every $h\in\mathbb Z[X]$ whose reduction modulo $q$ has positive degree, is separable, and is coprime to $\mathrm{avoid}$, the ring $A/(P+(h(u)))$ is nontrivial and is formally unramified over $\mathbb Z$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$q$ half of the statement that level sets of the modular unit $\Delta(\tau)/\Delta(q\tau)$ on the component of the mod-$q$ fibre of the model of $X_0(N_0q)$ cut out by the chosen minimal prime are nonempty and unramified. It feeds [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval), which supplies the pool of closed points used in the construction of relative Picard data for the model.
